--TEST--
A `require` whose path is not known while compiling is `E0330` at the path, in the statement and the value form, and the literal form of the same path compiles — `rule:statements/require-is-the-only-inclusion-construct`
--FILE--
<?nvs
require Core\Path::thisDir() . '/lib/setup.nvs';

string $dir = 'lib/';
mixed $v = require $dir . 'setup.nvs';

// The control: text joined with `.` is known while compiling, so it reports nothing.
require './lib/' . 'setup.nvs';
--FILE lib/setup.nvs--
<?nvs
echo "setup ran\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0330]: the path of this `require` is not known while compiling
  --> %s:2:9
  |
2 | require Core\Path::thisDir() . '/lib/setup.nvs';
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no file can be loaded for this path
  = help: write the path as text, such as `require './autoload.nvs';`. A relative path starts from the folder of the file that contains the `require`

error[E0330]: the path of this `require` is not known while compiling
  --> %s:5:20
  |
5 | mixed $v = require $dir . 'setup.nvs';
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no file can be loaded for this path
  = help: write the path as text, such as `require './autoload.nvs';`. A relative path starts from the folder of the file that contains the `require`

